sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% Figure 15: Staff Management Sequence Diagram
    %% Verified against dashboard pages proxy.ts middleware layout guards

    actor S as Staff
    participant SD as Staff Dashboard /dashboard
    participant SA as Supabase Auth
    participant SC as Supabase Client browser
    participant SSR as Supabase Server server component
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Supabase
    participant RLS as Row Level Security Policies

    S->>SD: Opens /dashboard or /login
    alt Not authenticated
        SD-->>S: Redirect to /login
        S->>SD: Enters credentials demo admin@aura.com
        SD->>SA: signInWithPassword email password
        SA-->>SD: Returns user session
        SD->>SD: Check staff table for user_id
        alt Staff record exists
            SD-->>S: Grants dashboard access
        else No staff record
            SD->>SA: signOut
            SD-->>S: Redirect to /portal This account does not have staff access
        end
    else Already authenticated
        SD->>SA: getUser validate session
        SA-->>SD: Returns user
    end

    SD->>SSR: Server-side layout check getUser staff lookup
    SSR->>SA: Validate session cookie
    SA-->>SSR: Returns authenticated user
    SSR->>DB: SELECT staff WHERE user_id = auth.uid()
    RLS-.->DB: policy staff_select_self
    DB-->>SSR: Returns staff row
    SSR-->>SD: Renders dashboard layout

    S->>SD: Views dashboard overview
    SD->>SC: SELECT patients count head
    SC->>DB: Query patients table
    RLS-.->DB: policy staff_manage_patients
    DB-->>SC: Returns patient count
    SC-->>SD: Returns count
    SD->>SC: SELECT appointments today count
    SC->>DB: Query appointments today
    DB-->>SC: Returns today count
    SC-->>SD: Returns count
    SD->>S: Displays stats upcoming appointments

    alt Patient Management
        S->>SD: Navigates to /dashboard/patients
        SD->>SC: SELECT patients ORDER BY created_at DESC
        SC->>DB: Query patients table
        DB-->>SC: Returns patient list
        SC-->>SD: Returns patients
        SD->>S: Displays patient directory

        rect rgb(240, 248, 247)
        note right of SD: CRUD Operations
        alt Create Patient
            S->>SD: Opens /dashboard/patients/new
            S->>SD: Fills patient form name email phone etc
            SD->>SC: INSERT INTO patients form data
            SC->>DB: Insert patient row
            DB-->>SC: Confirm insert
            SC-->>SD: Redirect to patient list
        else View Patient Details
            S->>SD: Clicks patient record
            SD->>SC: SELECT patients WHERE id = patientId
            SC->>DB: Query patient by ID
            DB-->>SC: Returns patient and appointments
            SC-->>SD: Returns patient data
            SD->>S: Displays patient details
        else Update Patient
            S->>SD: Opens /dashboard/patients/edit/id
            S->>SD: Edits patient details
            SD->>SC: UPDATE patients SET WHERE id = patientId
            SC->>DB: Update patient row
            DB-->>SC: Confirm update
            SC-->>SD: Redirect to patient list
        else Delete Patient
            S->>SD: Clicks delete on patient
            SD->>S: Confirm deletion dialog
            S->>SD: Confirms
            SD->>SC: DELETE FROM patients WHERE id = patientId
            SC->>DB: Delete patient row
            DB-->>SC: Confirm deletion
            SC-->>SD: Redirect to patient list
        end
        end
    else Appointment Management
        S->>SD: Navigates to /dashboard/appointments
        SD->>SC: SELECT appointments WITH patients ORDER BY scheduled_at ASC
        SC->>DB: Query appointments joined patients
        DB-->>SC: Returns appointments patient names
        SC-->>SD: Returns appointments
        SD->>S: Displays appointment schedule

        rect rgb(240, 248, 247)
        note right of SD: CRUD Operations
        alt Schedule Appointment
            S->>SD: Opens /dashboard/appointments/new
            S->>SD: Selects patient treatment date time duration
            SD->>SC: INSERT INTO appointments patient_id treatment_type scheduled_at duration notes
            SC->>DB: Insert appointment row
            alt Conflict overlap detected
                DB-->>SC: Error slot conflict
                SC-->>SD: Conflict detected
                SD->>S: Shows error reloads page
            else Success
                DB-->>SC: Confirm insert
                SC-->>SD: Redirect to appointments
                SD->>S: Displays updated schedule
            end
        else Edit Appointment
            S->>SD: Opens /dashboard/appointments/edit/id
            S->>SD: Edits treatment duration time status notes
            SD->>SC: UPDATE appointments SET WHERE id = appointmentId
            SC->>DB: Update appointment row
            alt Conflict overlap detected
                DB-->>SC: Error slot conflict
                SC-->>SD: Shows conflict warning
                SD->>S: Blocks save
            else Success
                DB-->>SC: Confirm update
                SC-->>SD: Redirect to appointments
                SD->>S: Displays updated schedule
            end
        else Update Status
            S->>SD: Changes status button scheduled confirmed completed cancelled
            SD->>SC: UPDATE appointments SET status WHERE id = appointmentId
            SC->>DB: Update appointment status
            DB-->>SC: Confirm update
            SC-->>SD: Optimistic UI update
        else Delete Appointment
            S->>SD: Clicks delete on appointment
            SD->>S: Confirm deletion dialog
            S->>SD: Confirms
            SD->>SC: DELETE FROM appointments WHERE id = appointmentId
            SC->>DB: Delete appointment row
            DB-->>SC: Confirm deletion
            SC-->>SD: Redirect to appointments
        end
        end
    end

    S->>SD: Clicks Sign Out
    SD->>SA: signOut
    SA-->>SD: Session cleared
    SD-->>S: Redirect to /login

    note over RLS,DB: RLS policies enforce staff access to records linked to authenticated session Direct table access not RPC is used for staff operations
